    <div class="section-body">
      <p class="section-intro">City names are not random: streets and parks are often zero article, while theatres, cinemas, hotels and many named bridges often use <code>the</code>. The safest strategy is to notice the type of place and learn the fixed exceptions.</p>
      <table class="reference-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Usually zero article</th><th>Pattern</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Streets, roads, avenues</td><td>Proper name + street word</td><td>Oxford Street, Baker Street, Fifth Avenue, Wall Street, Broadway</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Parks and squares</td><td>Proper name + park/square/garden as part of the name</td><td>Central Park, Hyde Park, Trafalgar Square, Times Square, Covent Garden</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Some iconic bridges</td><td>Older/fixed names without article</td><td>Tower Bridge, London Bridge, Brooklyn Bridge in many route-style contexts</td></tr>
